From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sven Panne <sven.panne@checkmk.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:48:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(format): leave the content of string literals alone

IndentationComments and IndentationClosingBraces, which run on every
--format, and the fix of ConsecutiveBlankLines work line by line. They
took lines inside multi-line strings ("""...""", '''...''', /.../ and
$/.../$) for code: a line starting with // was indented like a comment,
a lone } was aligned with a { before it, and blank lines were removed.
Braces in comments and in multi-line strings also threw off the search
for the matching brace.

CodeNarc checks ConsecutiveBlankLines, NoTabCharacter and
TrailingWhitespace line by line, so it reports whitespace in strings,
too, and fixing it changed the values of the strings. Other fixes, like
the ones of IfStatementBraces and Indentation, could change strings as
well.

getLinesInfo() scans the source like the Groovy lexer does, so that
these fixes know which lines start inside a string or a comment, which
braces belong to the code, and which parts of a line are string
content. Violations of the whitespace rules in string content are
filtered out like the ones disabled by comments, NoTabCharacter only
replaces the tabs outside of strings, and a fix which would still
change the value of a string literal is not applied.
---
